course: dictionary
lesson: 13966
title: Words about where we come from
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Your lineage is the line of family members who came before you: your parents, your grandparents, your great-grandparents and everyone further back.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «Her family tree showed a lineage of farmers that went back five hundred years.» The words family tree and back through the years tell you that lineage means your family line from long ago.
explain: Lineage has a science meaning too. Living things that come from the same ancestor belong to one lineage, so scientists can follow the lineage of a animal back over millions of years.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put «family line» in place of lineage. If the sentence still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Lineage is a noun: one lineage, several lineages.
fact: «Lineage» means the line of your ancestors, the family members who came before you.
fact: «Ancestor» means a family member who lived long ago, such as a great-grandparent or someone further back.
fact: In science, a lineage is a line of living things that descend from a common ancestor.
fact: Lineage tells the reader where someone comes from, which is why it appears in history, family studies and the Bible.
exercise: «The king proudly traced his lineage back to a warrior from long ago.» What does lineage mean here? | A large castle with many rooms | A battle won in winter | A type of royal crown | *The line of family members who came before him
exercise: «Scientists traced the lineage of the bird back to one common ancestor.» What does lineage mean in this sentence? | A feather that falls to the ground | A group of birds flying south together | *A line of living things that come from one common ancestor | A bird's nest made of twigs
exercise: «Her lineage can be traced back to Scotland.» Find and copy the word that means the family line. | *lineage | traced | Scotland | back
test: «Mia's family tree showed a lineage of teachers stretching back four generations.» What does lineage mean? | A school trip to the museum | *The line of family members who came before her | A tall tree in the garden | A new puppy in the family
test: Which meaning of lineage belongs to science? | A line of people waiting for a bus | A set of steps leading up a hill | A list of the best school marks | *A line of living things that descend from one common ancestor
exam: Priya says lineage is just a fancy word for family. Why is that only half right? | *It is the line of family members who came before you, and in science it is a line of living things from a common ancestor | It only means your parents | It only means your grandparents | It means a family holiday
